# Local .terraform directories
**/.terraform/*

# .tfstate files
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*

# Crash log files
crash.log

# Ignore any .tfvars files that are generated automatically for each Terraform run. Most
# .tfvars files are managed as part of configuration and so should be included in
# version control.
#
# example.tfvars

# Ignore override files as they are usually used to override resources locally and so
# are not checked in
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json

# Include override files you do wish to add to version control using negated pattern
#
# !example_override.tf

# Saved plan output from `terraform plan -out=tfplan`.
#
# Uncommented 2026-08-24. A saved plan is not a summary -- it embeds the fully
# resolved values it intends to apply, including outputs marked `sensitive`,
# which for this configuration means the backup-relay and backup-auditor IAM
# secret access keys in the clear. The rule shipped commented out as an example,
# so a plan file left in the tree was untracked rather than ignored and would be
# swept up by `git add -A` into a public repository.
*tfplan*

# Bootstrap config — contains all tokens and credentials, never commit
bootstrap/config.json

# Talos secrets and generated configs — store offline, never commit
.talos/
*.age.key
talosconfig
secrets.yaml

# Age private keys
*.key
!.sops.yaml

# Ansible retry files
*.retry
ansible/.ansible_retry

# Security review notes — local only, never published.
# This repository is public; review findings name live, unremediated weaknesses
# and must not leave the workstation. Keep the working copy at
# docs/security-review.md and reference it from committed docs by name only,
# never by quoting its contents.
docs/security-review.md
docs/security-review-*.md
# Same rule, different name. The 2026-08-25 review was filed as
# docs/cluster-review-<date>.md, which matched neither pattern above and so sat
# untracked rather than ignored -- one `git add -A` away from being published to
# a public repo. Match on the shape of the name, not one chosen spelling of it.
docs/cluster-review*.md
docs/*-review-????-??-??.md
# Findings files, same rule again. An earlier ignore for these was lost from the
# working tree before it was ever committed, which is its own argument for
# keeping the pattern broad: the protection is only real once it is in git.
# Anything named for findings, anywhere under docs/, at any depth.
docs/**/*finding*
docs/*finding*
findings*.md
